00:11:41.634 --> 00:11:42.168
- OK.

00:11:42.802 --> 00:11:44.704
- Take me to your leg workout.

00:11:45.638 --> 00:11:48.340
- Mmm, which one? Squats? 

00:11:48.441 --> 00:11:49.842
- Tell me, tell me the routine.

00:11:50.476 --> 00:11:55.715
- Routine, you know, quads. 
Obviously quads. Hamstrings— 

00:11:55.715 --> 00:11:57.116
- How much pride do you take in your quads?

00:11:57.116 --> 00:12:01.954
- It was never a thing at all. 
Like, everyone said I had big legs, 
but it was never, like, a thing, 

00:12:01.954 --> 00:12:04.724
and people weren’t obsessed with it 
till I got to the NFL. 

00:12:04.724 --> 00:12:11.063
Now, like, if I wear short shorts—like, I’ll walk 
in an airport, and old ladies would come up to me 
and be like,“Oooh, you got nice legs.”

00:12:11.063 --> 00:12:14.066
Before that, it was never like, 
“Oooh, you have nice legs.”

00:12:14.066 --> 00:12:15.034
I always just had legs.

00:12:15.401 --> 00:12:18.304
- Take me to your go-to karaoke song.

00:12:18.971 --> 00:12:20.639
- It's Mario, “Let Me Love You.”

00:12:20.639 --> 00:12:21.574
- How do you sing the song?

00:12:22.575 --> 00:12:23.209
- Tryin’ to get me.

00:12:24.710 --> 00:12:27.079
[Singing] Baby, I just don't get it.

00:12:27.079 --> 00:12:28.347
I ain’t gonna give you too much.

00:12:28.347 --> 00:12:30.883
- Oh, come on! You have to 
at least do one line.

00:12:30.883 --> 00:12:34.587
- Listen, listen, cuz my singing, my rapping career 
is gonna come on a little bit later so I can’t—

00:12:34.587 --> 00:12:35.821
- Oh, so you gotta wait. 

00:12:35.821 --> 00:12:37.990
- Gotta keep ‘em tuned in, you know? 
You feel me? Just a little bit.

00:12:39.759 --> 00:12:41.327
I kinda got you, lowkey. I ain’t gonna lie.

00:12:41.560 --> 00:12:44.330
- I know, I don't—like, it doesn't matter 
what I do, you're gonna win. 

00:12:44.330 --> 00:12:45.865
- Yeah, just lettin’ you know.

00:12:46.766 --> 00:12:51.337
- Well, you know, you know 
Christian McCaffrey’s still up, so it's cool.

00:12:51.871 --> 00:12:54.240
Christian McCaffrey’s still the better 
Connect Four player. 

00:12:54.840 --> 00:12:56.776
- That's crazy you brought that back up, not gonna lie.

00:12:57.042 --> 00:12:58.010
That’s a smart move.

00:12:58.010 --> 00:12:59.712
- I thought maybe if I distracted you—

00:12:59.712 --> 00:13:00.679
- Yeah, yeah, I like that.

00:13:00.679 --> 00:13:02.081
- Ah, you saw what I was doing.

00:13:05.050 --> 00:13:05.718
Good for you.

00:13:07.353 --> 00:13:08.687
You're the better Connect Four player.

00:13:10.623 --> 00:13:11.624
Yay.

00:13:12.725 --> 00:13:13.259
- Pushups.

00:13:13.459 --> 00:13:14.560
- Thanks for doin’ the interview.

00:13:14.560 --> 00:13:15.227
- No, pushups.

00:13:15.427 --> 00:13:16.195
- No.

00:13:16.228 --> 00:13:17.229
- Did you not agree to that?

00:13:17.229 --> 00:13:17.763
- I'll do one.

00:13:18.264 --> 00:13:18.864
- Five. 

00:13:19.298 --> 00:13:20.633
I don't even know if I can do one. 

00:13:21.534 --> 00:13:23.602
- Down. I’ll count that. 

00:13:23.602 --> 00:13:24.904
Two. I count that. 

00:13:25.104 --> 00:13:28.808
Three. Four. Five.

00:13:28.808 --> 00:13:30.476
- There you go. 
- There you go. 

00:13:30.709 --> 00:13:31.710
- I need to work on my form.

00:13:36.649 --> 00:13:37.650
Saquon.

00:13:37.883 --> 00:13:38.884
- What’s good?

00:13:38.884 --> 00:13:46.625
So it has been, like, a couple weeks since 
I interviewed you in L.A., and two days 
after our interview, Odell got traded. 

00:13:46.926 --> 00:13:48.127
- It's sad to see him go. 

00:13:48.127 --> 00:13:51.831
Every time people come ask me, 
“How you feel about Odell?”

00:13:51.831 --> 00:13:53.766
Like, obviously, that's my boy. I'm upset.

00:13:53.766 --> 00:13:59.405
Like, I don't think anyone's gonna sit out here 
and say, “Oh, we're happy Odell got traded,” 
but at the same thing, it’s a business. 

00:13:59.772 --> 00:14:02.007
And, you know, we gotta continue to work. 

00:14:02.007 --> 00:14:04.109
- OK, so have you seen Odell since?

00:14:04.276 --> 00:14:06.946
- We hung out. It didn’t feel real. 

00:14:07.479 --> 00:14:12.017
It was like, dang. He walked in, like, with a Cleveland 
shirt cuz he was just done working out.

00:14:12.585 --> 00:14:14.820
And I was like, “Dang, 
you over here in a Cleveland shirt already.”

00:14:14.820 --> 00:14:18.090
You never know. 
One day hopefully we can compete 
in a Super Bowl one day. 

00:14:18.090 --> 00:14:21.794
- So if Odell’s not on the team anymore, 
I mean, what happens to the dancing?

00:14:21.794 --> 00:14:24.630
- Oh, we gonna try to get Eli along 
with some dance moves soon. 

00:14:24.630 --> 00:14:29.435
- All right, now lastly, I have to ask. 
Now Baker and Odell are on a team together. 

00:14:29.768 --> 00:14:31.437
Do you feel a little left out?

00:14:33.405 --> 00:14:36.642
- No, no. You know, 
I do not feel left out at all. 

00:14:37.243 --> 00:14:37.977
I'm happy for those guys. 

00:14:38.611 --> 00:14:40.813
- All right, we're going to wrap 
this video up with a selfie. 

00:14:40.813 --> 00:14:44.683
- We have Rookie of the Year right here,
who was just fantastic in this interview.

00:14:44.683 --> 00:14:45.217
How’d it feel?

00:14:45.217 --> 00:14:46.652
- Thank you so much, it was amazing.

